      "writtenOn": "2026-02-26T04:48:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That will defer the preemption control from kernel to userspace. The `size` per ioctl call will be critical for userspace. If it\u0027s too large, the preemption will not work, if it\u0027s too small, the syscall overhead are increased.\n\nFor the ioctl interface, how about keep current ZRAM_ANDROID_IOC_PROCESS_WRITEBACK for the whole process and add a new cmd like ZRAM_ANDROID_IOC_PROCESS_WRITEBACK_PARTIAL to support the start_addr, size, end_addr?",
      "parentUuid": "1ccd11c3_8a0281c1",
      "revId": "f4b4ea5a7169c4319a806161d2f49fd0a8e40bc5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
